{"id":"15.6.6","doc":"T","title":"Interrupt upon Unauthorized PIF Access Alignment","words":269,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Access to all of ESP32-S3's modules/peripherals (excluding RTC FAST memory and SLOW memory) is word aligned."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"ESP32-S3 can be configured to check the access alignment to all modules/peripherals, and trigger Interrupt upon non-word aligned access."}]},{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"This interrupt corresponds to the CORE_m_PIF_PMS_MONITOR_VIOLATE_SIZE_INTR interrupt source described in Table 9.3-1 from "},{"t":"xref","id":"9","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Chapter 9"}]},{"t":"text","v":" Interrupt Matrix (INTERRUPT)."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Note that CPU can convert some non-word aligned access to word aligned access, thus avoiding triggering alignment interrupt."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Table 15.6-6 below lists all the possible access alignments and their results (when interrupt is enabled), in which:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"INTR: interrupt"}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"√: access succeeds and no interrupt."}]}]}]]},{"t":"table","caption":"Table 15.6-6. All Possible Access Alignment and their Results","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"Accessed Address"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Access Alignment"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Read"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Write"}]],"rows":[{"n":8,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"0x0"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Byte aligned"}],[{"t":"text","v":"INTR"}],[{"t":"text","v":"INTR"}]]},{"n":9,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"0x0"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Half-word aligned"}],[{"t":"text","v":"INTR"}],[{"t":"text","v":"INTR"}]]},{"n":10,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"0x0"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Word aligned"}],[{"t":"text","v":"√"}],[{"t":"text","v":"√"}]]},{"n":11,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"0x1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Byte aligned"}],[{"t":"text","v":"INTR"}],[{"t":"text","v":"INTR"}]]},{"n":12,"c":[[{"t":